  "version": 1,
  "description": "Frozen Muse lane-row validation vectors (mirror of Codex+Claude pack 2). Offline only: every payload below is a frozen model-usage-telemetry wire body run through the pure contract consumer (no HTTP, no live catalogue, no roster write). The muse source binds the roster's enabled Muse row (muse-spark-1.3-contributor, cliproxy-meta lane per the reviewed roster) the way pack 2 binds its two lanes. Cases pin model id, lane binding (evidence source), snapshot expiry, reset-countdown derivation and preference, serviceable/state agreement, and weekly-window projection. Each case lists the exact expected outcome; the spec asserts full equality so behavior drift in either direction fails loudly. Foreign-row markers (oc/gpt-5.6-codex, oc/claude-sonnet-5) are opaque stand-ins for other lanes' rows, borrowed only to prove they never project onto the Muse source.",
  "clocks": {
    "observedAt": "2026-09-10T12:00:00.000Z",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-10T12:01:05.000Z",
    "note": "Fetched 65s after observed. Countdown cases exploit the gap: an observedAt-anchored derivation differs from a fetch-anchored one, so the exact expected value proves which clock the consumer uses."
